room tavern "The Salty Keel"
  bg bg_tavern_wide
  width 2560
  music music_tavern
  ambience tavern
  grade "brightness(0.95) saturate(0.85)"
  # Calibrated against the bar (~1.1 m), the barrels and the seated regulars.
  perspective horizon 450 ref 875 height 440
  scale 705 268
  scale 792 426
  scale 880 585
  # Stops in front of the barrels, the regulars' table and the foot of the bar, which runs
  # diagonally from (1330,712) to (1800,880).
  walk (470,875) (640,790) (820,772) (850,705) (985,705) (1000,736) (1320,738) (1610,837) (1600,880)
  entry 1060,850

  # Atmosphere: lanterns over the bar, candles on the tables, the lamp by the hearth.
  footsteps wood
  light 930,205 radius 120 lantern
  light 1198,285 radius 110 lantern
  light 905,322 radius 80 lantern
  light 1070,350 radius 80 lantern
  light 890,368 radius 60 candle
  light 1190,378 radius 70 candle
  light 2350,215 radius 160 lamp

  # Full-figure art behind the bar; the counter (occluder) hides her below the waist. Her
  # feet sit just behind the occluder's floor line, so she's scaled up to read at the
  # bar's real depth.
  sprite npc_marta_body_v2 at 1960,728 size 1.12 idle speaker marta for marta grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"
  # Seated at his own table in the corner by the door, off the walkable floor.
  sprite npc_rook_body at 545,805 size 0.82 flip idle speaker rook for rook grade "saturate(0.75) sepia(0.12) brightness(0.82)"
  # At the corner table with Rook, out of uniform, facing him across it.
  sprite npc_bramwick_seated at 760,812 size 0.8 flip idle speaker bramwick for bramwick_t grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"
  # Ashore, standing behind his navigator's table.
  sprite npc_ansel_body at 640,748 size 1 idle speaker ansel for ansel_t grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"
  # Up at the bar for his dawn toast.
  sprite npc_silas_body at 1250,742 size 1 idle speaker silas for cray_t grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"
  # At the back, in his old customs waistcoat, once the inquiry has begun.
  sprite npc_dorrit_body at 905,690 size 1 idle speaker dorrit for dorrit_t grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"
  # Hobb, ashore once the flag's down, at the foot of the bar, showing the room his arm. His art
  # stops at the shins, so his feet sit just below the frame and the scene's edge hides the cut.
  sprite npc_hobb_body at 1760,884 size 0.8 flip idle speaker hobb for hobb_t grade "saturate(0.85) sepia(0.08) brightness(0.9)"

  occluder floor 730 (1308,568) (2560,590) (2560,880) (1800,880) (1328,716)

  scene if act 4 and not inquiry_done and has ledger and has purse and has claims_book and not cray_toast
    set cray_toast
    say "Cray is at the bar in a coat worth more than the bar. He's buying drinks to the Marrow. Nobody drinks them."

  hotspot marta "Marta"
    area 1885,340 160x245
    stand 1500,800
    look "Marta runs the Salty Keel, and by most accounts Port Vela. She's won several arguments today and is pacing herself."
    talk "I catch Marta's eye. It takes some catching."
      talk tavernkeeper
    give "She only takes things worth trading."
    open "Marta is not a door. She has made this clear to several people, one of them a door."
    state if act 4 and ledger_written and not seen:marta4.ending
      talk: talk marta4 at ending
    state if act 4 and iou_paid
      talk: talk marta4 at cards
    state if act 4 and ledger_written
      talk: talk marta4 at ending
    state if act 4 and quarantine_lifted
      talk: talk marta4 at book
    state if act 4 and inquiry_done
      talk: talk marta4 at after
    state if act 4
      look "Marta's behind the bar, polishing the glass she had when I left for the Straits. She's watching the door. She doesn't trust it."
      talk "She points at me with the glass before I'm halfway across the room."
        talk marta4

  hotspot rook "old sailor"
    area 420,435 240x375
    stand 940,835
    look "An old man with a mug he stopped drinking an hour ago. He sits very still. His nose says he used to drink more."
    talk "He looks up before I speak. He's been waiting."
      talk rook
    give "He waves it away without looking at it."
    state if act 4 and purse_given
      name "Old Rook"
      look "Rook at his corner table, upright for once. A drink he isn't drinking, and Bramwick for company."
      talk: talk rook4 at hub
    state if act 4
      name "Old Rook"
      look "Rook's got company: Bramwick, out of uniform, matching him drink for drink and apology for apology."
      talk "He sees my face and puts his mug down very slowly."
        talk rook4
    state if met_rook
      name "Old Rook"

  hotspot bar "the bar"
    area (1310,568) (2500,588) (2500,700) (1330,712)
    stand 1420,780
    look "A bar polished by a thousand elbows and one very committed mop. The bottles are arranged by how much trouble they cause."
    use "I'd need money, and the customs house pays its clerks in experience."
    open "It's a bar, not a crate."

  hotspot door_out "door to the docks"
    area 40,220 380x450
    stand 590,835
    exit dock
    look "The door out to the docks. Cooler out there."

  hotspot crowd "the regulars"
    area 1000,510 300x200
    stand 1150,760
    nowalk
    look "Sailors and dockhands, drinking to the Marrow. Half wish her luck. The other half have bets on a slate that says she won't come back."
    talk "I ask about the Straits. Three of them go quiet at once. It's a local custom."
    use "There's a betting slate on their table. It's missing something official."
    state if act 4 and wager_paid
      look "The regulars, lighter by three years' wages and cheerful about it. They're toasting the Marrow. Properly, this time."
      talk "They raise their mugs at me before I'm halfway there."
        talk regulars4 at after
    state if act 4 and wager and quarantine_lifted
      look "The regulars are reading the betting slate like men who just heard a ship come in."
      talk "I go over and tap the slate, under SHE COMES BACK."
        set wager_paid
        talk regulars4 at pay
    state if act 4 and wager
      look "The regulars. My three years' wages are on their slate, stamped, under SHE COMES BACK. They keep not catching my eye."
      talk "I go over to the slate. Several of them discover something interesting in their mugs."
        talk regulars4 at owe
    state if act 4
      look "The regulars, drinking to the Marrow. They use the tone for a ship that isn't coming back. Cray told them what's aboard, so nobody looks."
      talk "I tell them she's back. They tell me that's very kind, and buy me a drink in her memory."
    state if wager
      look "The regulars have my three years' wages on their slate, stamped. They keep toasting me, which is either friendly or premature."

  hotspot bramwick_t "Bramwick"
    show if act 4
    area 690,440 150x340
    stand 1040,835
    look "Bramwick, suspended and out of uniform, at Rook's table. Without his coat he looks like a man let out of a small room."
    talk "He straightens up as though I'm an inspection."
      talk bramwick4
    give "“I can't accept anything, Fenn. I'm suspended. I can barely accept this drink.”"
    # Order matters (the first match wins): the unpaid IOU first, then the card game it
    # leads to, then plain reinstatement.
    state if quarantine_lifted and not iou_paid
      name "Harbourmaster Bramwick"
      look "Harbourmaster Bramwick, back in his coat, touching it as if it might come off again."
      give "“Not now, Fenn. I'm on duty again, and I've only just remembered how.”"
      talk: talk bramwick4 at debt
    state if iou_paid
      name "Harbourmaster Bramwick"
      look "Bramwick at cards with Marta, holding his hand close to his coat. The coat is on. So is everything else, by the look of him."
      give "“Not now, Fenn. I'm losing, and it's taken thirty years to get this good at it.”"
      talk: talk bramwick4 at cards
    state if inquiry_done
      name "Harbourmaster Bramwick"
      look "Harbourmaster Bramwick, back in his coat, touching it as if it might come off again."
      give "“Not now, Fenn. I'm on duty again, and I've only just remembered how.”"
      talk: talk bramwick4 at after
    state if seen:bramwick4.badly
      talk: talk bramwick4 at hub

  hotspot ansel_t "Ansel Fenn"
    show if act 4 and quarantine_lifted
    area 600,395 120x305
    stand 1040,835
    look "My father, ashore, arms wide over Rook's table. He's telling Rook a story Rook was there for. Rook lets him."
    talk "He turns round, beaming, before I've said a word."
      talk ansel4 at ashore
    give "“Keep it, son. I've got everything I came ashore for, and a navigator besides.”"

  hotspot hobb_t "Hobb"
    show if act 4 and quarantine_lifted
    area 1660,410 200x470
    stand 1560,860
    look "Hobb, sleeve up, letting the regulars read his arm. Under TAM, fresh and swollen: HOME. The ink is worse than ever."
    talk "He holds his arm out before I've said a word, like a man showing his papers."
      talk hobb4
    give "“Don't give me things, clerk. I'll only want them inked.”"
    state if seen:hobb4.room
      talk: talk hobb4 at again

  hotspot cray_t "Silas Cray"
    show if act 4 and not cray_gone and (inquiry_done or has ledger) and (inquiry_done or has purse) and (inquiry_done or has claims_book)
    area 1190,440 130x300
    stand 1120,770
    look "Silas Cray at the bar, raising a glass to the window and the ship outside. Dawn bell in one pocket, the harbour in the other."
    talk "He turns, already smiling."
      talk inquiry
    give "“Save it for the inquiry, clerk. Oh, don't look so surprised. I always know when I'm about to be inquired into. It's a gift.”"
    state if inquiry_done
      talk: talk inquiry at waiting

  hotspot dorrit_t "Dorrit"
    show if act 4 and inquiry_started
    area 855,470 110x220
    nowalk
    look "Dorrit, at the back, guarding the punch bowl. He has stamped his own cup."
    talk "“Stamped and passed, clerk. I'm only here as a witness. And for the punch. I'm told customs inspected the rum personally.”"

  use stamp on crowd if act 4 and wager
    "My bet's on the slate already, stamped. The ink is dry. The Marrow is wet. Both count."
  use stamp on crowd if act 4
    "Every bet says she won't come back. She's anchored outside the window. Betting now would be robbery, and I'm the honest one tonight."
  # Giving the stamp back: Bramwick lifts the quarantine.
  use stamp on bramwick_t if inquiry_done and not quarantine_lifted
    "I hold out the harbour stamp, handle first, the way you'd hand back a sword."
    set quarantine_lifted
    sound chime
    talk bramwick4 at stamp
  # He stamps the lifting order and lends the stamp straight back for the ledger.
  use stamp on bramwick_t if not inquiry_done
    "“Put that away, Fenn. I'm suspended. If I so much as touch it, Cray will have me for theft of my own stamp.”"
  use stamp on bramwick_t if not ledger_written
    "“Use it first, Fenn. Then bring it back. The book's waiting.”"
  use stamp on bramwick_t
    "He waves it off. “Keep it till dawn. A clerk without a stamp looks undressed.”"
  # The ledger, corrected at the bar in front of everyone.
  use stamp on ledger if quarantine_lifted and not ledger_written
    "I lay the ledger on the bar. The room notices before I've opened it."
    talk ledger4
  use ledger on bar if quarantine_lifted and not ledger_written
    "I lay the ledger on the bar. The room notices before I've opened it."
    talk ledger4
  use ledger on bar if inquiry_done and not quarantine_lifted
    "Not with a yellow flag on the boom. The Harbourmaster lifts it, and his stamp is in my pocket."
  use ledger on bar if not ledger_written
    "Not yet. Until Marta says otherwise, this book is evidence. You don't write in evidence. You hold it up."
  use ledger on bar
    "It's written. I keep opening it to check. It's still written."
  use purse on rook
    "He shakes his head. “Hold on to it, boy. Hand it back to me in front of everybody. That's the only way I can take it.”"
  use ledger on bramwick_t if ledger_written
    "He reads the new line with his hat in both hands, the way men read a name on a church wall."
  use ledger on bramwick_t if inquiry_done
    "“Under my lie, Fenn, not over it. I want people to be able to read both.”"
  use ledger on bramwick_t
    "He looks at his own handwriting and goes grey. “Yes. That's my lie. Bring it to the inquiry, Fenn. I'll stand next to it.”"
  use ledger on marta if ledger_written
    "She reads my entry, then reads it again, which for Marta is a standing ovation."
  use ledger on marta if inquiry_done and not quarantine_lifted
    "“Not yet, clerk. Give Bramwick his stamp back and get that flag down. Then write in it, here, in front of everybody.”"
  use ledger on marta if inquiry_done
    "“Don't show me, clerk. Write in it. The bar's right there, and so is everybody.”"
  use ledger on marta
    "She pushes it back across the bar without opening it. “Not to me, clerk. To him, in front of me.”"
  use purse on marta
    "“Not to me, clerk. To him, in front of me. And let Rook do the handing. It's his to give back.”"
  use purse on bramwick_t
    "He won't touch it. “That's Rook's to give back, Fenn, not mine to take. I've taken quite enough off that man.”"
  use claims_book on bramwick_t
    "He finds Vane's refusal, then six payouts on the facing page. He closes the book gently. “That's the kind of paper, Fenn.”"
  use kelp_manifest on bramwick_t
    "He reads “for fog” twice. “Somebody at Cray's writes down what he's told. When this is over, bring me that clerk.”"
  use claims_book on marta
    "She runs a finger down the page and stops at Vane's name. “Refused. I remember the month she drank that refusal. Keep it, clerk.”"
  use ansel_log on rook
    "He finds his own name in it and reads the line twice. “He wrote I was a good navigator. He always was a terrible liar.”"
  use kelp_manifest on marta
    "She reads “for fog”, and laughs out loud, once, like a cork. “Keep that for afters.”"
  use ledger on cray_t
    "He raises his glass to it. “To the ledger. Long may it say what it says.”"
  use rum on marta
    "“Inspected? With a crowbar? Best customs has done for me in thirty years.” She uncorks it over the punch. “His key. Tell Bramwick to bluff.”"
    take rum
    give drawer_key
    set marta_paid
    note marta_key "Marta won Bramwick's drawer key and wouldn't give it back for nothing. One bottle of her impounded rum, for the punch, was the rate."
    sound pickup
  use stamp on crowd if not wager
    "Every bet on that slate says the Marrow won't come back. Somebody ought to take the other side."
    talk regulars
  use stamp on crowd
    "My bet's on the slate, stamped and drying. There's no taking it back, which is the point of ink."
